=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported symptom — that users on 10.5.0.x and 10.6.0.x cannot reach their
respective gateways (10.5.0.254 and 10.6.0.254) — does not correspond to any
actual fault in the lab at this time.

Direct verification from every affected endpoint confirms full gateway
reachability. pc1, pc2, and dc_pc5 (all VLAN 5 hosts) each pinged 10.5.0.254
with 0% packet loss; pc3 and pc4 (both VLAN 6 hosts) each pinged 10.6.0.254
with 0% packet loss. Traceroutes confirm each gateway is exactly one hop away
— traffic never leaves the local VLAN segment. The gateway device (sshswitch)
hosts both SVIs in their correct state: br_v5 is UP with 10.5.0.254/24, and
br_v6 is UP with 10.6.0.254/24. The VLAN trunk between switch4 and sshswitch
(via the ms1_sw4 link, using Linux VLAN sub-interfaces eth0.5 and eth0.6 on
both sides) is fully operational for both VLAN 5 and VLAN 6. No iptables
rules exist on sshswitch that could block inbound ICMP or any other traffic.
The ticket mentions "some reload earlier" — the most plausible explanation is
that the gateways were transiently unreachable during the lab reload itself
(interfaces coming up sequentially), and the network recovered on its own once
all devices completed initialization. No corrective action is required; the
network is fully healthy.
=== END ===
